  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -28,9 +28,33 @@ https://www.wireshark.org/certifications[the Wireshark Foundation].\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+This release fixes an API/ABI change that was introduced in Wireshark 4.6.1, which caused a compatibility issue with plugins built for Wireshark 4.6.0. wsbuglink:20881[].\n \n-// * wssalink:2025-07[] {notable}\n+The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+\n+* wssalink:2025-07[] {notable}\n+HTTP3 dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:20860[].\n+// cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 9139917bd8\n+// Fixed in release-4.6: 38df909ca8\n+// Fixed in release-4.4: 3911b2958d\n+// CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\n+// CWE-1325\n+// * HTTP/3 dissector freezes on a large number of headers. wsbuglink:20860[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2025-08[] {notable}\n+MEGACO dissector infinite loop.\n+wsbuglink:20884[].\n+// cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: aba1fbe626\n+// Fixed in release-4.6: 4f79070084\n+// Fixed in release-4.4: e4f3706e1b\n+// AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H\n+// CWE-835\n+// * Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-11-30-12267984256.pcap. wsbuglink:20884[].\n+\n+// * wssalink:2025-09[] {notable}\n // Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n // wsbuglink:xxx[].\n // cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n@@ -48,10 +72,17 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n // Bugs with the {notable} attribute show up in the \"What's Changed\" box on the download page.\n //* Wireshark contains traces of nuts. What kind of nuts? The kind you're allergic to. wsbuglink:5000[] {notable}\n \n+* ws_base32_decode should be named \\*_encode ? wsbuglink:20754[].\n+* Omnipeek files not working in 4.6.1. wsbuglink:20876[].\n+* Stack buffer overflow in wiretap/ber.c (ber_open) wsbuglink:20878[].\n+* Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-11-30-12266121180.pcap. wsbuglink:20883[].\n \n // == Known Bugs\n \n-// === New and Updated Features\n+=== New and Updated Features\n+\n+* The Windows installers now ship with the Visual C++ Redistributable version 14.44.35112.\n+  They previously shipped with 14.40.33807.\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n \n@@ -64,43 +95,29 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.6.1.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n+// rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.6.2.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-802.11 Radiotap\n-AC DR\n-ASN.1 BER\n-ASN.1 PER\n-BPv7\n-BT L2CAP\n-CFM\n-Darwin\n-DNS\n-DTLS\n-EAPOL-MKA\n-HTTP\n+ATM PW\n+COSEM\n+COTP\n+DECT NR+\n+DMP\n+Fc00\n+GTP\n HTTP3\n-ISObus VT\n-KRB5\n-LTP\n-NAS-EPS\n-NETDFS\n-NMEA 0183\n-P1\n-RPC_NETLOGON\n-RTSE\n-SGP.22\n-SGP.32\n-SMB\n-SNMP\n-TCP\n-TECMP\n-TFTP\n-VLAN\n-WINREG\n-X509AF\n-X509SAT\n-ZBD\n+IEEE 802.15.4\n+ISIS HELLO\n+ISOBUS\n+MAC-LTE\n+MAUSB\n+MEGACO\n+MPEG DSM-CC\n+OsmoTRXD\n+PTP\n+SAPDIAG\n+SMTP\n+RLC\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
